{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro","id":1033427,"title":"\u200bPanscrypias and Keepers of the Word as Dragon Parts (NECRO)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-17T10:13:06-08:00","id":1033427,"title":"\u200bPanscrypias and Keepers of the Word as Dragon Parts (NECRO)","content":"<br /> Diamond Order love their \u2018Atlantean Dragon\u2019 analogy. All of true \u2018Atlanteans\u2019 are one Dragon of Magic, swiping in to Fallen World to remember it that Magic is Alive and Glorious and Supernal will rule over world again, one day. Or something like that.<br /> <br /> In modern nights, Diamond Order ascribe to this \u2018Dragon Parts\u2019 connotations:<ul><li>Adamantine Arrrow \u2013Talons of Dragon</li> <li>Guardians of Veil - Eyes of Dragon</li> <li>Mysterium \u2013 Wings of Dragon</li> <li>Silver Ladder \u2013 Voice of Dragon</li> </ul>Of four, Mysterium\u2019s analogy is extremely fitting, as Order tires to \u2018rise\u2019 the Art in to new highest. It\u2019s also fitting with ot being compromised of previous two proper Orders \u2013 Pancryptias and Keepers of the Word \u2013 as two Wings of one Dragon. But Diamond Alliance is much older than Mysterium \u2013 Mysterium was created in circa 1200 CE and Diamond as Alliance is coming from at least circe 200 BCE. It\u2019s almost 1400 years where there where Five Diamons Orders \u2013 and this Diamond also followed Dragon Analogy \u2013 and with Pancryptias and Keepers in place of Mysterium \u2013 I cannot imagine that Pancryptias and Keepers simply said \u2018okay, you are Left Wing of Dragon, we are Right Wing of Dragon\u2019. <b>What do you think would be those ancient Orders Dragon Parts analogy?</b><br /> <br /> To help maybe better imagine them, I quote <b>DaveB</b>\u2019s post about both Pancryptias and Keepers nature in 2E background.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember what the Corpus Mysterium is about<b></b>: Neither Order had the tone statement the Mysterium does of &quot;magic is alive&quot;, because that was her Noumenon.<br /> <br /> The Keepers believed that they safeguarded *knowledge*, and had both proto-Athenea that didn't have the religious traits modern Athenea have, and a Guanxi-like economy of information. They thought that they were the last bastions of civilisation in a chaotic universe, and their internal disagreements were about whether it was better to influence Sleeper affairs by sharing technology and culture the Sleepers had lost versus preserving it for future need. They were like a cross between the Mysterium, Free Council, and Silver Ladder, with almost Seer-like leanings. Their tone statement could be &quot;magic has worth&quot; - both a price to be paid and value if taken from others.<br /> <br /> The Pancryptiates were smaller, weirder, and much more gnostic. They believed Sleepers actively damaged the world by existing, and sought to either remove themselves from the world and society or build bulwarks where the Abyss had less sway. The Keepers regarded all knowledge as at least partially magical - the Pancryptiates would be outraged by a Keeper storehouse keeping roman crop management manuals alongside the grimoires. They built demesnes, summoned supernal entities, studied the Abyss, explored Emanations and sought a way *out* of the Fallen World. They were like a cross between the Mysterium, Guardians, Arrow (they relished self-sacrifice for the cause, like becoming savants or jettisonning all mortal ties) and, in some ways, Tremere - they were deeply interested in the soul, and thought the world was evil.<br /> <br /> In a medieval setting, the Keepers would be monasteries and the Pancryptiates hermitage-dwelling poor friars.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:23:35-08:00","id":1033436,"title":"","content":"When the Mysterium was two Orders the alliance of Orders was the Pentacle, not the Diamond. The FC essentially stepped in and filled that slot after the creation of the Mysterium so it's likely only one of the two original Orders (Probably the Keepers) of the Mysterium were considered the Wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:44:01-08:00","id":1033456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted