please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:21:59-08:00","id":1034164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1034137#post1034137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want disquieting? I'll give you disquieting.<br /> <br /> Where exactly did you think the whole Dragon symbolism motif came from, anyway?<br /> <br /> (That's right! The Diamond got it from the Tremere!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I died and I'm buried! My favorite part of Diamond imagery is Tremere doing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Now I need to flog myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:11:45-08:00","id":1034201,"title":"","content":"So with the '<b>Mage </b>reveal of the month', we still can return to topics question - <b>What Dragon Parts would be Panscryptias, Keepers of the Word and ( I'm not believing I'm writing this ) Tremere as Diamond Orders?</b><br /> <br /> Blood of Dragon is Silver Ladder mythical bloodline from Atlantis they look for. I suspect, Tremere being all about souls and Dragons could really usurp title like Soul of Dragon? Or maybe Heart of Dragon? Panscryptias sounds to me as more reclusive types - so maybe Tail of Dragon? Keepers of the Word seems to be most 'logical' of Orders - so maybe Brain of Dragon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:03:52-08:00","id":1034229,"title":"","content":"Voice of the Dragon is the Silver Ladder. The Tremere are clearly the Blood of the Dragon.<br /> <br /> I suspect the Keepers were the original Wings of the Dragon, with the Pancryptias possibly being the Shadow of the Dragon or some such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}