":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:46:30-08:00","id":1034256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1034244#post1034244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I prefer that to it being the Atlantean nobility.</div> </div> </div> </div>They weren't nobility, they were the priests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:55:34-08:00","id":1034266,"title":"","content":"Priest-kings. They took the idea from Plato, who wanted a noble caste who believed wholeheartedly that working for the common folk was their natural role and duty, and to have them see this as a noble burden rather than a source of personal privilege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:07:44-08:00","id":1034276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1034249#post1034249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't like an Order of proximi trying to get their blood across the world and extinguish the Sleeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be fine, but the references to the Blood of the Dragon are largely as a positive thing that no longer exists. There are even suggestions that the difference between the Exarchs and the Oracles is that the latter are the true noblility.<br /> <br /> I dunno, it's just a bit too close to real life Nazi conspiracy for my liking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They weren't nobility, they were the priests. </div> </div> </div>In 1e 'The Blood of the Dragon' are referenced in a couple of places as the possible name of the Atlantean Noblility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:13:51-08:00","id":1034277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1034276#post1034276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, it's just a bit too close to real life Nazi conspiracy for my liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does sound like it gave the Orders some motivation.<br /> <br /> I can't blame them for claiming it was some mythical Oracles and not reapers. They'd hardly want to advertise it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:56:22-08:00","id":1034301,"title":"","content":"Keepers sounds cooler than Mysterium, from what I see.<br /> Also, I really want that Tremere-Gnosis-Thing to be finally out :&lt;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T01:47:32-08:00","id":1034486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1034301#post1034301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keepers sounds cooler than Mysterium, from what I see.<br /> Also, I really want that Tremere-Gnosis-Thing to be finally out :&lt;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, Dave please give us the new Tremere, its been almost a year since you first spoiled that!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T03:08:09-08:00","id":1034499,"title":"","content":"To ease discussion, Blood of the Dragon sidebar from <b>Silver Ladder </b>book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silver Ladder, p. 44</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Blood of the Dragon</b><br /> When the order gives public talks about reviving an Atlantean state, it usually leaves out one important ancient position: the monarch. Legends say Atlantis had kings and queens who ruled all the orders, though scholars sometimes postulate that the royal \u201cBlood of the Dragon\u201d were only ceremonial overlords, objects of devotion who left governance to other mages. Monarchy is an unpopular concept in the modern age, so th\u00e9archs often avoid discussing it at all, but not all of them personally object to reviving the royal line \u2014 provided they could find its heirs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of all the orders, the Ladder knows the most about the Blood of the Dragon, but even its knowledge is filled with apocrypha. Many believe the royal line died with Atlantis. Nobles stayed with their sinking towers or met their end by Exarch treachery. Some say the Blood are the Exarchs, that the royal house betrayed humanity, but the order dislikes the implications of this story because it calls Atlantis\u2019 virtues into question. A more positive spin says the Oracles are five siblings of the Blood who have vowed to save the human race. The Merovingian Proximi (see pp. 66\u201368) claimed they had the Dragon\u2019s Blood, but the Ladder doesn\u2019t believe them.<br /> <br /> Prophecies say the Blood of the Dragon still walk the world as a sixth order, hiddenin the shadows of the others. Princes monitor the world\u2019s Consilii, waiting for the day that mages prove themselves worthy. They study the secret gifts of the Dragon\u2019s Blood \u2014 and perhaps they guard a final Watchtower of ultimate Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the bold statements in 8<sup>th</sup> Century of Tremere when they join as Order and connection to Final Watchtower \u2013 I COULD see Tremere saying that they are Blood of Dragon. But then their heretical bend uncovered In 1099 would mean so much blow to Silver Ladder forcing this idea, that Tearchs would not recover from this as \u2018political visionary of Diamond\u2019. Then I would probably point Tremere as Soul of Dragon \u2013 pointing new direction in Middle Ages for whole Diamond and connected to finding their Final Watchtower \u2013 but not making claims as large as Blood of Dragon themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Interesting Fact:</b> Numa and whole The Sanguine Laurel cabal from Boston setting are claiming <i>they are</i> Blood of Dragon, hailing from the Atlantis itself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-19-2017, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T03:44:25-08:00","id":1034511,"title":"","content":"Tremere would still work as the Blood of the Dragon, heck they made up the dragon imagery, and there's a good chance they claimed to be that. The sidebar even mentions that Prophecies say the Blood of the Dragon are still out there as a sixth Order hidden in the shadows. That sounds like the Tremere to me. Since the Tremere were exposed the SL have gone back and either edited, denied or destroyed those things that might have backed up the Tremere claim which is why they now have multiple theories and most of their info is apocrypha. Plus you say it would be too big a blow to the SL politically, but I say that there is a masterful PR legacy that could make all of that go away: Logophages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T03:52:25-08:00","id":1034514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1034511#post1034511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremere would still work as the Blood of the Dragon, heck they made up the dragon imagery, and there's a good chance they claimed to be that. The sidebar even mentions that Prophecies say the Blood of the Dragon are still out there as a sixth Order hidden in the shadows. That sounds like the Tremere to me. Since the Tremere were exposed the SL have gone back and either edited, denied or destroyed those things that might have backed up the Tremere claim which is why they now have multiple theories and most of their info is apocrypha. Plus you say it would be too big a blow to the SL politically, but I say that there is a masterful PR legacy that could make all of that go away: Logophages.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we ( as modern day Awakened ) KNOW that Tremere were Sixth Order. There are Mysterium ( previous Keepers of Words ) records on this. Heck, we can have Time mages touch some medival armor and SEE how in 1099 on Antioch Convocation Tremere were declared worst type of Left Handed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>If Tremere even once were declared Blood of Dragon, this event would be know to any Diamond members from then on.</b> OR Tremere never where officially declared Blood of Dragon - only <i>plotting to be</i> it, in their secret circles when they consumed next Reapers on their lists. But if they were never official Blood of Dragon, they would use other title in their Dragon Symbology, publicly - it's their that introduced it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T04:03:47-08:00","id":1034516,"title":"","content":"They would only know that Tremere were once considered the Blood of the Dragon until their heresy was discovered and they were renounced. Now they're seeking the &quot;true&quot; Blood of the Dragon, but that's just propaganda because they probably already found it in the Tremere hence why the prophecies seem to keep making veiled references to them.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that public opinion is more mutable than time and politicians like the SL mold it all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:17:28-08:00","id":1034649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1034229#post1034229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect the Keepers were the original Wings of the Dragon, with the Pancryptias possibly being the Shadow of the Dragon or some such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading today about Egregore ( that was Panscryptias invention ) I would rather point to them being Wing. But for me, both Panscryptias and Keepers do not work with Wing symbology - it does have sense <i>after</i> change in to Mysterium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mysteriorum Exemplum, p. 102 of Mysterium book</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Phrases:</b> \u201cI\u2019m a member of the Mysterium!\u201d More subtle, the character learns that working <i>wing</i> into conversation marks him as a member of the order: \u201cI do love to see birds take wing, don\u2019t you?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:56:38-08:00","id":1034675,"title":"","content":"The Keepers would be the Wings because of the two they're the most expansive, and at least on the surface we're the most similar to the Mysterium as it is today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:12:10-08:00","id":1035263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1034137#post1034137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want disquieting? I'll give you disquieting.<br /> <br /> Where exactly did you think the whole Dragon symbolism motif came from, anyway?<br /> <br /> (That's right! The Diamond got it from the Tremere!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. That's... Unexpected. Now that you mention it, though, I never did actually notice how incongruous the inclusion of dragons in the symbolism of Atlantis was. It wasn't something I questioned when the book treated the Fall as literal history but, when it's a metaphor cobbled together from borrowed Classical philosophy and mythology, dragons don't really &quot;fit&quot; anywhere. <br /> <br /> Even more noticeable, none of the mythologies they draw upon view dragons favourably. Vritra, Tiamat, Typhon...<br /> <br /> That's going in my &quot;Things to mull&quot; pile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T01:08:31-08:00","id":1036491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1035263#post1035263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. That's... Unexpected. Now that you mention it, though, I never did actually notice how incongruous the inclusion of dragons in the symbolism of Atlantis was. It wasn't something I questioned when the book treated the Fall as literal history but, when it's a metaphor cobbled together from borrowed Classical philosophy and mythology, dragons don't really &quot;fit&quot; anywhere.<br /> <br /> Even more noticeable, none of the mythologies they draw upon view dragons favourably. Vritra, Tiamat, Typhon...<br /> <br /> That's going in my &quot;Things to mull&quot; pile.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I thought mages using the dragon imagery was an allusion to the Asian dragons, who are dangerous but still divine beings, where Hellenistic mages used the Astral to communicate with their Asian counterparts. How naive I was.<br /> <br /> This thread is giving me the shudders.<br /> <br /> By the way, didn't Dave also mention that the 2E Tremere would be more like a separate template, much like the Pure are to the Forsaken, or am I dreaming it up in feverish excitement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T02:56:24-08:00","id":1036511,"title":"","content":"The Tremere already were sort of their own mini-template in 1e, as of Left Hand Path. They can essentially enter Torpor, use souls for power, and develop what amounts to a second Legacy drawn from a Legacy they devoured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T05:12:58-08:00","id":1036548,"title":"","content":"Yeah - in 2e, Tremere are a modified Template that alters how their Gnosis works and gives them their other powers like not-Torpor and burning the soul currently attached to them for life. The Houses are their equivalents of Legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:03:57-08:00","id":1036565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1036548#post1036548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah - in 2e, Tremere are a modified Template that alters how their Gnosis works and gives them their other powers like not-Torpor and burning the soul currently attached to them for life. The Houses are their equivalents of Legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When can we expect the update to 2ed for the tremere. Im dying to know more about them and to play one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:38:23-08:00","id":1036579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1036548#post1036548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah - in 2e, Tremere are a modified Template that alters how their Gnosis works and gives them their other powers like not-Torpor and burning the soul currently attached to them for life. The Houses are their equivalents of Legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it seems that the niche for Vampire-Mage hybrids for 2E, in the vein of the Admonitoria, has been officially filled.<br /> <br /> I'd love it if they have means consume and render down souls to Mana like how vampires convert blood to Vitae, and for stealing Awakened souls to function as the Tremere equivalent to diablerie. Discipline-equivalents can be House Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:44:55-08:00","id":1036585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1036491#post1036491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I thought mages using the dragon imagery was an allusion to the Asian dragons, who are dangerous but still divine beings, where Hellenistic mages used the Astral to communicate with their Asian counterparts. How naive I was.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <b>Hermit</b>, you are right - <b>What about whole Mantra Sadhaki and their Naga Kingdom influence of Awakened in Alexandrian times?</b> In the end, Diamond Order were using Estern philosophy for their final creation around Roman Golden, so Asian mages influences on Western Orders must be earlier.<br /> <br /> I could see Tremere later joining the Diamond and saying 'we all are <i>really</i> decedents of Dragons', but first idea on Dragon Orders Symbology should come from Indian mages and their Naga Kingdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-23-2017, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:53:31-08:00","id":1036588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1036585#post1036585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, <b>Hermit</b>, you are right - <b>What about whole Mantra Sadhaki and their Naga Kingdom influence of Awakened in Alexandrian times?</b> In the end, Diamond Order were using Estern philosophy for their final creation around Roman Golden, so Asian mages influences on Western Orders must be earlier.<br /> <br /> I could see Tremere later joining the Diamond and saying 'we all are <i>really</i> decedents of Dragons', but first idea on Dragon Orders Symbology should come from Indian mages and their Naga Kingdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where were the Mantra Sadhaki based off culturally, and the Naga Kingdom come from in real life again? I'm asking this 'cuz I don't remember clearly. I was under the impression the Great Cult was from the Hindu and/or Southeastern cultures, and they don't hold serpents in <i>that </i>much regard... Although that bit about the Naga Kingdom has me confused. I should refresh my knowledge on Dark Eras (and mythos on the Naga)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:06:16-08:00","id":1036594,"title":"","content":"They are Hindu Great(est) Cult. And basically worship Dragons as messengers between High and Low Worlds, with closest thing to modern Atlantis - Naga Kingdom - before the concept itself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Eras, p. 93</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mantra Sadhaki</b><br /> <i>Exiles from the Kingdom of Dragons</i><br /> Look at humanity in the Kali Yuga: mostly Asleep and cursed with mortal fragility. It was not always so. In the prior age, superhuman tribes carved the world into warring kingdoms. They were violent, but even their evil was wiser than contemporary good. They knew when they sinned. Instead of confusion about their purpose, they felt afraid to embrace it.<br /> <br /> Of all demigod nations, the greatest was the Naga Kingdom. The Naga people took their name from the serpentine gods they worshiped, who taught them the elemental Paths and the way of civilization long before the other tribes, and might have served as fathers and mothers to them all \u2014 in ancient times, the line between blood heritage and teachings was vanishingly thin. One of the five great bloodlines produced Prince Aryaka, and his great-granddaughter Kuni gave birth to the Pandavas: the fathers of civilization.<br /> <br /> Nagas battled their Pandava relatives, but also forged alliances with them to help them fulfill their destinies. Yet even in triumph, the Nagas felt loss, for the Pandavas were destined to leave lesser descendants. They helped the Pandavas build mighty cities in the Khandava Forest, and suffered as the mortal race declined \u2014 and, on several occasions, betrayed them. Finally, the time came to withdraw heroic power from the Pandavas. The Mahabharata says a snake killed Arjuna\u2019s grandson, bringing the Age of Iron to the world. The Naga tribe also withdrew, but gave its teachings to a line of ascetics, the Mantra Sadhaki, to continue the task of guiding ordinary humans toward righteousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:22:22-08:00","id":1036602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1036594#post1036594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are Hindu Great(est) Cult. And basically worship Dragons as messengers between High and Low Worlds, with closest thing to modern Atlantis - Naga Kingdom - before the concept itself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>good graces</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least they have a damn good in-universe mythos to back them up. That alone satisfies me.<br /> <br /> Then I'll just step back and shudder once again at the awesome (in more ways than one) implications of all this new information about the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:58:43-08:00","id":1036625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033427-\u200bpanscrypias-and-keepers-of-the-word-as-dragon-parts-necro?p=1036565#post1036565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When can we expect the update to 2ed for the tremere. Im dying to know more about them and to play one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I know, but again, I'm saying Dark Eras 2 would be a lovely place for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writin